# ==============================================================================
# RELZZY ARCADE // SOUND SYSTEM CONFIGURATION (.env.example)
# ==============================================================================
#
# NOTE: The core YouTube playlist functionality uses the official YouTube
# IFrame Player API and runs COMPLETELY WITHOUT an API key!
#
# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 1. YOUTUBE PLAYLIST CONFIGURATION
# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Put your YouTube Playlist ID or full playlist URL here.
# Supports raw IDs (e.g., PLw-VjHDlEOgvtnnnqWlTqByAtC7tXBg6D) or full URLs:
#   https://www.youtube.com/playlist?list=PLw-VjHDlEOgvtnnnqWlTqByAtC7tXBg6D
#
YOUTUBE_PLAYLIST_ID=PLw-VjHDlEOgvtnnnqWlTqByAtC7tXBg6D

# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 2. OPTIONAL YOUTUBE DATA API v3 KEY
# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Only needed if you wish to pre-fetch extended playlist track metadata (titles,
# thumbnails) ahead of time using the YouTube Data API v3.
#
# SECURITY & DEPLOYMENT INSTRUCTIONS FOR STATIC SITES (relzzy.fun):
# Because this website is hosted statically (GitHub Pages / Cloudflare Pages),
# any API key defined in client-side JavaScript is publicly visible in the browser.
#
# If you choose to use an API key on a client-side static site:
#   1. In Google Cloud Console, create a new API Key for "YouTube Data API v3".
#   2. Under "Application restrictions", choose "HTTP referrers (web sites)".
#   3. Add your exact allowed domains:
#        https://relzzy.fun/*
#        http://localhost:* (for local development)
#   4. Under "API restrictions", select ONLY "YouTube Data API v3".
#
# Alternatively, deploy a light serverless proxy (Cloudflare Worker or Vercel
# Serverless Function) to keep the API key completely hidden on the server side.
#
YOUTUBE_API_KEY=YOUR_API_KEY_HERE
